SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO KEISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, YOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYAMA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI, HIDESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, TAMAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOGI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, KEISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>In a step of manufacturing an image creating device (electron beam device) comprising an electron emitting device, specifically surface conduction electron emitting device, a face-plate electrode (72) and a wiring (74) of an electron source substrate (71) on which the wiring and a device electrode are formed are opposed to each other and projections are eliminated by applying a predetermined voltage between the wiring (74) and the electrode (72) and causing electric discharge previously. By thus subjecting an electric field applying process to the electron source substrate (71), the factor of electric discharge, such as projections in the electron source, caused when the electron beem device represented by an image creating device is constituted and driven is eliminated, and therefore, the image creating device has a good display performance without any unlit pixel on a display image even after a long time image display.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Pour fabriquer un imageur à canon d'électrons comprenant un dispositif émettant des électrons, en utilisant un dispositif d'émissions d'électrons à conduction de surface, on prend une électrode à plaque de façade (72) et un câblage (74) d'un substrat de source d'électrons (71) sur laquelle le câblage et l'électrode du dispositif sont opposés l'un à l'autre, on arrive à éliminer les projections par application d'une tension entre le câblage (74) et l'électrode (72) ce qui provoque une décharge électrique préalable. Ainsi en soumettant le substrat de la source d'électrons (71) à un processus d'application d'un champ électrique, on élimine le facteur de décharge électrique, tel que la projection dans la source d'électrons imputable à la constitution et au pilotage du canon d'électrons de l'imageur, ce qui fait que l'imageur a un bon rendement d'affichage sans qu'aucun pixel soit éteint à l'affichage de l'image, même après un long temps d'affichage de l'image.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>